cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyMack in your research, please cite the archived release below."
title: "pyMack: Local linear stability of compressible and hypersonic boundary layers"
abstract: >-
  pyMack is an MIT-licensed Python package for local linear stability theory
  of compressible and hypersonic boundary layers. It provides base-flow
  generation, temporal and spatial eigenvalue solvers, discrete-mode
  diagnostics, growth and neutral curves, N-factors, and structured CPU batch
  sweeps. The repository carries layered tests, a 37-case verification
  registry with provenance-tracked regeneration records, measured benchmark
  provenance, examples, and reproducibility instructions.
type: software
